# shellcheck — shell lint configuration (see modules/formatter.nix)
#
# Most shell here is a fragment readFile'd into writeShellApplication rather
# than a standalone program, so it has no shebang for shellcheck to read the
# dialect from. `shell=bash` sets the default; the fragments also carry a
# `# shellcheck shell=bash` directive on line 1 so editors agree without
# needing this file.
shell=bash

# No rules are disabled. writeShellApplication runs shellcheck at build time
# too, so anything silenced here would still fail the package build — keeping
# the two in agreement matters more than a quiet lint run.

# Do not follow `source` into files outside the checked set; the fragments
# source nothing, and following store paths would be non-reproducible.
external-sources=false
